Sanity Check System Tests
========================

This directory contains tests for the sanity check system introduced in QE.

Test Files:
-----------

1. sanity_close_atoms.in
   - Tests detection of atoms that are too close together
   - Two Si atoms only 0.5 bohr (~0.26 Å) apart
   - Should trigger CRITICAL warning

2. sanity_extreme_cell.in
   - Tests detection of extreme cell parameters
   - Cell with 10:1:1 aspect ratio
   - Should trigger INFO warning about extreme aspect ratio

3. sanity_isolated_atom.in
   - Tests detection of isolated atoms
   - Two Si atoms in a large cell, far apart
   - Should trigger WARNING about isolated atoms

4. sanity_force_continue.in
   - Tests command-line flag handling
   - Two Si atoms critically close (0.25 bohr apart)
   - Used to test --force and --ignore-sanity-checks flags

Running the Tests:
-----------------

# Normal run (should prompt on critical issues)
pw.x -input sanity_close_atoms.in

# Skip sanity checks entirely
pw.x -input sanity_close_atoms.in --ignore-sanity-checks

# Run sanity checks only (no calculation)
pw.x -input sanity_close_atoms.in --sanity-checks-only

# Change default configuration
pw.x --config sanity_checks.enabled=false

Expected Behavior:
-----------------

1. Default behavior: Sanity checks run, warnings shown on stderr, calculation continues
2. With --ignore-sanity-checks: Skip all checks
3. With --sanity-checks-only: Run checks and exit without calculation
4. Configuration changes persist across runs
5. All sanity check output goes to stderr, not stdout